summary:
  A held M mutes, unmutes and mutes again with the key's repeats.

history:
  A held key repeats some 25 times a second, and the branch had no guard:
  a second's hold was 26 toggles, and where it ended was the luck of the
  count.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FullRepresentation.qml

find:
              if (!event.isAutoRepeat) root.setUserVolume(playMusicOutput.volume > 0 ? 0 : root.targetVolume())

replace:
              if (!event.isAutoRepeat || true) root.setUserVolume(playMusicOutput.volume > 0 ? 0 : root.targetVolume())

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_m_held_down_is_one_mute.
  The behaviour itself is tests/qml/tst_heldkey.qml::test_m_held_down_mutes_once,
  on a copy of the handler. Line-neutral.
